WEBVTT

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:03.976
The domain Eukarya is split into four kingdoms.

00:00:03.976 --> 00:00:07.685
A useful way to compare them is how they get energy.

00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:11.820
Autotrophs make their own food, usually by photosynthesis.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.885
Heterotrophs have to get their food from other organisms.

00:00:16.592 --> 00:00:21.532
Protista is the catch-all kingdom for eukaryotes that don't fit anywhere else.

00:00:21.532 --> 00:00:26.662
Most are single-celled, like amoebas, and they can be autotrophs or heterotrophs.

00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:30.705
Fungi, like mushrooms and yeasts, are heterotrophs.

00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:35.032
They release enzymes and absorb nutrients from their surroundings.

00:00:35.732 --> 00:00:41.382
Plantae are multicellular autotrophs that make their own food through photosynthesis.

00:00:42.098 --> 00:00:50.048
Animalia are multicellular heterotrophs that eat other organisms, and most of them can move around at some point in their lives.
